      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "According to [[credential-scoping]], the Anthropic API key is **injected into the environment of spawned agent child processes immediately before they start**, not held by the Hub itself.\n\nSpecifically, the page describes that:\n\n- A local secrets loader reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup\n- The key is injected only into the spawned Ingest agent\u0027s child process environment\n- The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated\n- The same scoping model applies to the Query agent \u2014 it also receives the credential injected into its own environment at spawn, never inherited from the Hub\n\nThis design ensures that a compromised or misbehaving Hub cannot leak the credential by inspecting its own environment variables, since the key exists only in the short-lived child processes that actually call the Anthropic API.",
